# Test cases

## feature-tests/
The living specification of __PROJECT_NAME__: one Markdown file per behaviour,
grouped by domain — `feature-tests/<domain>/FT-vX.Y.Z.T-NN-<slug>.md`, written
in Gherkin (Given / When / Then). The ID embeds the version that introduced the
test and never changes; later versions append themselves to `updated_in`.

- `automation: automated` — implemented in the project's e2e/integration
  framework; the test name contains the FT ID; `automated_by` points to it.
- `automation: manual` — executed by an agent or during UAT; evidence goes to
  `docs/plans/vX/test-report.md`.
- `status: deprecated` — behaviour removed; kept for history.

## unit-tests/
Unit test **code** lives next to the source, per the stack's convention.
`unit-tests/vX.Y.Z.T.md` maps each WBS goal of a version to the unit tests that
cover it.

Commands to run everything: `commands:` in `docs/04-conventions/testing.md`.
